{
  "title": "The Phantom — Lab",
  "description": "Experiments in light, depth and place: the Phantom particle toy rebuilt for the graphics card.",
  "intro": {
    "kicker": "The Phantom / Lab",
    "title": "A million\npoints of light.",
    "text": "Four small experiments that grew out of the particle toy on the home page — rebuilt for the graphics card, given a body, a camera and somewhere to be.",
    "hint": "Scroll to begin"
  },
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "ignite",
      "kicker": "00 / Ignite",
      "title": "Every mark,\na million points.",
      "text": "The original Phantom drew about two thousand dots on a canvas. Here every point is simulated on the graphics card, so the same marks can hold up to a million. Move through them, click to send a shockwave, and open the shutter to watch them as a long exposure would."
    },
    {
      "id": "sculpt",
      "kicker": "01 / Sculpt",
      "title": "Give the light\na body.",
      "text": "The flat marks are inflated into relief and photographed by a virtual camera that behaves like a real one: the focal lengths of my two lenses, focus that falls off the way a thin lens predicts, and out-of-focus points that open into nine-bladed bokeh."
    },
    {
      "id": "develop",
      "kicker": "02 / Develop",
      "title": "Photographs,\nwith depth.",
      "text": "Each photograph is rebuilt with its own depth. A depth network gives the shapes; the distances come from reading the frame: where the horizon sits, how tall a walker stands, what the LiDAR saw from the same spot. From where it was taken it matches the print, blur included; step aside and the scene opens up. Contours read it as a map of equal light, or of equal distance."
    },
    {
      "id": "atlas",
      "kicker": "03 / Atlas",
      "title": "Where the light\nwas.",
      "text": "Every frame was taken somewhere. The atlas starts from the whole planet and descends to the places I photographed, rebuilt from public airborne LiDAR. New York and San Francisco so far; more places will follow."
    }
  ],
